      "hints": [
        "Rewrite the numerator $1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta = (1 - \\sin^2\\theta) - \\sin^2\\theta = \\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta$.",
        "Replace the denominator $1 - \\sin^2\\theta = \\cos^2\\theta$.",
        "Divide term by term to obtain $\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} - \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = 1 - \\tan^2\\theta$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Express the numerator and denominator in terms of $\\cos^2\\theta$ using $\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta = 1$:\n$$\\text{LHS} = \\frac{1 - 2\\sin^2\\theta}{1 - \\sin^2\\theta} = \\frac{(1 - \\sin^2\\theta) - \\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta - \\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}$$",
        "Split into two fractions and simplify to reach the RHS:\n$$\\text{LHS} = \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} - \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = 1 - \\tan^2\\theta$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
