      "hints": [
        "Substitute the proven identity: $1 - \\tan^2\\theta = 2\\tan^4\\theta$.",
        "Rearrange into a quadratic in $\\tan^2\\theta$: $2\\tan^4\\theta + \\tan^2\\theta - 1 = 0$.",
        "Factorise $(2\\tan^2\\theta - 1)(\\tan^2\\theta + 1) = 0$ and solve for $\\theta$ in $0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 180^\\circ$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute the identity into the given equation:\n$$1 - \\tan^2\\theta = 2\\tan^4\\theta \\implies 2\\tan^4\\theta + \\tan^2\\theta - 1 = 0$$",
        "Factorise as a quadratic in $\\tan^2\\theta$:\n$$(2\\tan^2\\theta - 1)(\\tan^2\\theta + 1) = 0$$",
        "Solve for the valid roots (noting $\\tan^2\\theta + 1 > 0$ for all real $\\theta$):\n$$2\\tan^2\\theta = 1 \\implies \\tan^2\\theta = 0.5 \\implies \\tan\\theta = \\pm\\sqrt{0.5} \\approx \\pm 0.7071$$",
        "Find both solutions in the interval $0^\\circ \\le \\theta \\le 180^\\circ$:\n$$\\text{For } \\tan\\theta = \\sqrt{0.5}: \\quad \\theta = \\tan^{-1}(0.7071) \\approx 35.3^\\circ$$\n$$\\text{For } \\tan\\theta = -\\sqrt{0.5}: \\quad \\theta = 180^\\circ - 35.3^\\circ = 144.7^\\circ$$\n$$(\\text{Solutions: } \\theta = 35.3^\\circ, \\quad 144.7^\\circ)$$"
      ],
